# GitHub CODEOWNERS — see https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Reviewers listed here are auto-assigned on PRs that touch the
# matching paths. Branch protection on main requires at least one
# CODEOWNER approval before merge.
#
# This is the operational arm of the two-person release policy
# (docs/security/RELEASE-POLICY.md): the tagger of a release MUST
# NOT be the same person who approved the release PR.
#
# Membership is maintained on the team, not here — add or remove people
# at github.com/orgs/sonomoshq/teams/maintainers and every rule below
# follows. As of 2026-08-12 the team is all five organisation members.
#
# NOTE 2026-08-12: this file spent a while doing nothing. It named
# @sonomos-ai/maintainers — a retired organisation that returns 404 —
# and then, briefly, a @sonomoshq/maintainers team that did not exist
# yet. Both failed the same way, which is the part worth remembering: a
# CODEOWNERS team reference resolves as `@org/team`, not as a URL. It
# does not follow the redirect that keeps old repository links working,
# and it requires the team to exist, be visible (not secret), AND hold
# write access to this repository. When it resolves to nothing the rule
# is skipped, and the parse error appears only on the repository's
# CODEOWNERS settings page — never in a pull request. Nothing warns you.
#
# The team now exists with push access and all five members. If you ever
# rename it, make it secret, or drop its repository access, every rule
# below silently stops applying, and with it the "all CODEOWNER paths
# reviewed" branch protection RELEASE-POLICY.md leans on. Verify with:
#
#   gh api repos/sonomoshq/Locke-Extension/teams
#
# which must list `maintainers` with permission `push`.

